% Rx_ZrnGrOverflow.in = macos ZGD_test_files/tst_zrngr_overflow.in (db9236b), copied for the binding gates
% (mmacos tZrnGrRoundTrip, pymacos test_zrngr_roundtrip); GridFile is resolved from the cwd.
% tst_zrngr_overflow.in -- public gate for the grid-index overflow guard
% (macos 2026-10-10, surfsub.F).  Identical to tst_zrngr_roundtrip.in but
% GridSrfdx= 1.0E-10: the bilinear pixel index xi=(xData.rhom)/dAct is then
% ~1e10 for ordinary rays, so i0=IDFLOOR(xi) saturates to INT_MAX and
% i1=i0+1 wraps to INT_MIN, defeating the integer bounds test.  GATE:
% a PRE-FIX engine SIGSEGVs in INTNORM (GridMat indexed hugely out of
% bounds -- the must-fail leg); POST-FIX the float guard treats the ray as
% off-grid (fh=0), counts it (WARN / grid_idx_ovf_get > 0) and the trace
% completes (nPass 32168, grid inert).

        ChfRayDir=  0.0E+00  0.0E+00  1.0E+00
        ChfRayPos=  0.0E+00  0.0E+00  -5.0E+00
          zSource=1.0E+21

        BaseUnits=  m
        WaveUnits=  m

           IndRef=1.0E+00
           Extinc=0.0E+00
          Wavelen=1.0E-06
             Flux=1.0E+00

         Aperture=4.0E+00
         Obscratn=2.4E+00

         GridType=  Circular
         nGridpts=  256
            xGrid=  -1.0E+00  0.0E+00  0.0E+00
            yGrid=  0.0E+00  -1.0E+00  0.0E+00

